WEBVTT

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.730
<i>We're in position.</i>

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.740
Cheers!

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.310
We win again!

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:22.990
One victory after another!

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:25.820
We're undefeatable with Remedius on our side.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:31.770
I didn't think you'd have talent 
as a tactical commander.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.220
Thank you, Party Leader Zemunn.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.580
But it's simply because I like chells, 
and that happens to have been useful here.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.890
Why do you participate in this battle?

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.920
No one would blame you 
for going home to Tsevellen.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.400
Well...

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:58.730
It wasn't until I came to this nation
 that I discovered the truth.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:01.280
Jushiki was supposed to 
bring people happiness,

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.320
but it's being used for oppression.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.660
I can't allow such injustice.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.370
Injustice, huh?

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.390
Talk will change nothing.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.880
That's why action is necessary.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.550
But all our actions are based in force.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.310
Yes, but you use force 
for the right purposes.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.250
There are no other options.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:01.750
Father, I surrender myself to your hand.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:02.280
<b>Calm Days and Lonely Nights</b>

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.830
I prepare for anything and accept everything.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.760
May your soul be in me

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.340
and in all beings of your creation.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.300
What's wrong?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.450
I cannot.

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:23.930
To participate in the rituals of another 
religion would be to betray my homeland.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.100
Dude...

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.580
You shall drench your abundant 
body of dreams in blood,

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:35.100
and weave a robe of moonlight and stardust.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:40.440
There, idleness and transience vanish,

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:46.940
and the pale messengers forget their 
need to compare their own ferocity.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:52.470
Even joyous days are somehow sad.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:56.250
A child's dream being 
made true is not enough

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.710
to end the loneliness.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:05.020
I believe in love that is 
without reason, without words,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.040
with only passion.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.180
Youth was a scar.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.550
Naivety tumbles from immortality
 to the ephemeral.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.610
That fleeting eternity,

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:23.380
that smile of yours that perished so quietly,

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:28.040
is all that remains singing in my heart.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.880
It's a silly song that Premelena 
sang for a night chat.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.650
It ought to be fitting 
for this whiny occasion.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.420
That's it, huh?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:52.770
Sobbing cheap tears over a coworker's death?

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:54.510
How dare you?!

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.140
I'll kill you!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.270
You fools!

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.710
Gayus is right.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:02.090
Who killed our peer?

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.250
Our enemies are the damn Magatsushiki

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.410
and the Great Magatsushiki who control them,

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.700
Amupura and Janahn Ghalan.

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:09.780
Am I wrong?

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.170
All right, it's time to stop the tears.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.330
Who's going to kill them 
so our peer can rest in peace?

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:21.670
We are!

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.850
Then what are you waiting for?

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.170
Go to town!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.680
Hunt down every last damn Magatsushiki!

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.300
Send them back to hell where they belong!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.380
Sorry you had to play such a shitty role.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.820
That's why you called me, isn't it?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.650
What a pain in the ass you are.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:50.320
Say, why don't you take this 
opportunity to join our agency?

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.360
Huh?

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.040
I'm serious.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.970
I'm more interested in 
you two than you think.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.630
Sorry, Largonkin, but we like this

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.460
master-and-his-pet arrangement we have now.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.840
I agree with the pet over there.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:12.300
Am I not good enough to replace Diorg?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.410
Largonkin!

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.570
My apologies.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:18.710
Forget I said that.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.730
Oh, one thing.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.740
An acquaintance apparently 
saw Cuello in Eridana.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.840
I thought I should let you know.

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.420
Why is Cuello here?

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:40.250
<i>About the Aurora Hammer 
research you've requested...</i>

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.490
<i>It's quite dangerous.</i>

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:46.890
<i>There's a former Rahzel 
employee named Parumuwei</i>

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.260
<i>who currently sells weapons in Eridana.</i>

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.710
<i>Aurora Hammer is in contact with him.</i>

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:58.440
We just received the same 
information from the police.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:02.520
Are they in Eridana to obtain weapons?

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.050
<i>That's still hard to say.</i>

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.030
<i>I'm still searching for their hideout.</i>

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.820
<i>It seems someone up top is 
keeping control of information.</i>

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:13.500
Up top?

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.450
The police or military or something?

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.470
Gayus...

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:20.340
The missing man's on the 
other side of the street.

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.880
Egurrd.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.560
So you finally noticed.

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:44.560
That was quite an obvious way to draw us out.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.690
We're getting surrounded a lot today.

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:54.950
The world's just starting to 
take notice of my hidden charms.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.640
There are too many.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.080
It's a pain, but should we?

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.630
No, wait.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:04.010
Egurrd, you trapped us without attacking us

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:06.780
because you have no intention 
of killing us, correct?

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.850
The brass will meet with you.

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:11.110
Come with me.

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.850
Egurrd, that's not the right way to ask.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.980
"Please come with me."

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.180
I've brought them with me.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:34.110
Welcome, Offensive Jushikiists.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.240
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Gohhel.

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:42.000
I'm the director of Dragon's Jaw.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:46.090
Dragon's Jaw is the special force

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:49.370
established by Queen Xenobia of Ilm.

00:08:49.890 --> 00:08:53.010
No wonder you have the 
stench of a military man.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.410
What?

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:56.760
Only a man who's been in a field battle

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.510
takes a cigarette out of 
the bottom of the case.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:02.000
You should have told me sooner.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.140
You didn't notice? You idiot.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.650
By the way, there's a reason 
we revealed our hand.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.740
We want you to refrain from

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:15.640
any further involvement with 
Rahzel Company or the Aurora Hammer.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:20.840
Our mission is to eliminate the hostile 
activities against the Dragon Empire.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:24.250
We can't have amateurs getting in our way.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:25.450
I hope you understand.

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.810
I don't.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.880
Aurora Hammer is intent on taking 
down the dictatorship in Urmun.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.140
Dochetta is a thorn even 
for the Dragon Empire.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:39.870
So though the Dragon Empire
 might have cause to assist them,

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.430
you have no reason to defeat them.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.060
It is indeed an odd request.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:48.060
If there <i>was</i> a reason,

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.190
it would be because Viscount Remedius
 joined the Aurora Hammer.

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.210
Wait.

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:00.450
You're right.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:04.700
The viscount has come to 
sympathize with the Aurora Front

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:08.370
after seeing the misery 
in Urmun as a hostage.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.960
And to make matters worse...

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.060
Colonel!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.840
As soon as it was learned 
that Party Leader Zemunn

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.840
had started moving towards 
reconciliation with Dochetta,

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:21.770
they joined forces with a man named
Zhuo Lu and got rid of of Zemunn,

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:25.850
creating an even more extreme 
organization known as the Aurora Hammer.

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:29.600
A hostage took over an 
anti-government organization?

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.080
The viscount is Tsevellen.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:34.240
At this rate, it could be perceived

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:37.490
that the Dragon Empire is meddling 
in the internal affairs of Urmun.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.520
I see.

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:42.330
The raid during the hostage 
exchange was a distraction.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:46.870
Your real goal was the assassination 
of Viscount Remedius.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:49.290
That hostage exchange itself

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:53.260
was nothing but a show put on by 
Viscount Remedius to secure funds.

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:55.750
We simply took advantage of that.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:00.500
Did you put poison in the identifier device?

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:06.260
We thought we could take the opportunity 
to destroy Aurora Hammer itself.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.490
You understand now, do you not?

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:11.150
Let us deal with it from here.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:13.100
This isn't a request.

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.270
It's an order.

00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:19.790
To be clear, even if Calpulnia makes 
a tearful request for your help,

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:23.030
you have no need to oblige.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:25.280
That's all I have to say.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:29.400
Please don't forget that you're 
dealing with the government.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:47.290
That comes to 1,023,420,000 yen.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:49.430
Thank you very much.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:53.450
I'm impressed you hid all this, Parumuwei.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:56.400
I've heard that you're a 
former Rahzel employee.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.010
Yes, actually.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:03.460
But how do you intend to 
transport all of this?

00:12:03.940 --> 00:12:06.200
That's none of your business.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:12.000
S-Say, um...

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.730
Are you really going to buy this?

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:20.130
If you don't mind me saying, 
it's incomplete.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:24.460
Even Rahzel and the military abandoned it.

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:25.470
I don't care.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.720
You don't plan on using it, do you?

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.990
It's intended to be no more than a threat.

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:35.110
Besides, the composition shiki needs 
to be completed in order to use it.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.260
No...

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.340
Impossible...

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:42.140
You're...

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.750
You look like you don't know 
why you've been captured,

00:12:53.090 --> 00:12:56.250
Viscount Remedius Levvi Rahzel.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.130
You murderer!

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.960
Looks like you've still got some life in you.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:09.690
It seems the Dragon Empire royalty 
has a taste for wild kittens.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.640
Dochetta, what you're doing is wrong!

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.590
And?

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:22.150
What have you seen with your eyes?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.170
Fool.

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:29.530
No high-minded ideals or justice 
can save this nation anymore.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:33.740
I'll answer your question.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:37.310
You're a pestilence, Remedius.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:39.790
I'm not the only one who thinks so.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:45.920
I'll give you a special punishment.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.930
Die in the worst pain ever...

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:52.390
In despair!

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:04.530
Remedius no longer exists.

00:14:10.390 --> 00:14:12.530
Just shut up and have a seat.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.160
First, accounting.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:16.680
This is practically a kid's allowance book.

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:18.790
You waste too much money.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:22.060
Next, you're both grown-ups,

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:25.800
so at least pretend to be on 
good terms while you're working.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:31.930
Jeez, do the two of you 
never see eye to eye?

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:33.180
Nope.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:36.680
Just shake hands and make up.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:40.600
Huh? But I haven't fought with Gigina today.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.820
Then for the other day.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:47.850
Do it properly.

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:49.960
This is a Draken handshake.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:51.120
That's right.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.490
You do say the right thing 
every so often, Gigina.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.580
This isn't the right time 
to agree on something!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.800
There! Well done.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.380
Oh dear, look at the time.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.090
I have to get to work.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.340
Huh? I thought you had the day off.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:13.500
My boss and I are going to 
Rahzel Company tomorrow.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.130
We have a meeting about that.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:17.350
I'll be back for lunch.

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:18.670
Rahzel?

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.480
You're going to that island?

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:21.500
Yeah.

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:22.850
I'm kind of looking forward to it.

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:26.500
See you at our usual park this afternoon.

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:27.710
Okay.

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:30.380
And be sure to bring Mr. Gigina.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.240
Bye.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:36.870
You have it quite rough.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.870
Rahzel Company's gem supplement ring,

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:42.950
the Remetogen IV!

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.820
I said no!

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:51.130
You don't need it in battle, and it's 
not covered under work expenses.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:55.020
No wasting money.

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:57.420
It's Jabeira.

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:01.180
Well, if it isn't Gayus.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:04.510
Be cursed on the occasion of 
this coincidence, you bastard.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:10.030
Jabeira, your personality
changed mid-sentence.

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:12.590
You're so nitpicky, Iegie.

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:15.880
Either way, I ain't allowing that purchase.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:22.520
Is that guard ornament furniture 
craftsman Toldam's Lion Tooth?

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:25.580
You're pretty well-versed, 
for an uncultured Draken.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.540
Do you know which period it's from?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.120
Middle.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:35.300
In fact, it's from when he was 
working with painter Iem Adder.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.720
It's an exceedingly rare piece.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:43.310
We both have it rough, huh, nyoro?

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.180
You two seem to be doing well, though.

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.540
You seem to be happy.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.390
Are you not happy?

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:56.620
Well, our agency is like family.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.910
I divorced my husband and 
got fired from my job.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:03.330
I had nowhere to go when 
Chief Largonkin took me in.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:06.520
Iegie's story is similar.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:09.590
He adores Chief Largonkin like a father.

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:11.080
Family, huh?

00:17:11.080 --> 00:17:13.030
It's not bad, pyon!

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.150
Iegie, you'll lose money 
on that trade, nyoro!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.720
There. Repairs are all done.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:25.400
Damn, you went all-out

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:27.980
with seventh-order Jushiki on this thing.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.860
Of course it broke down.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.910
You swapped the engine chamber 
out with a Rahzel one, huh?

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:35.130
Yeah, are you upset?

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:37.740
No, good job.

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.750
Now, hand over that Majouken.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:45.500
Isn't that...

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:50.000
You had a part in the Magatsushiki 
incident, didn't you?

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.900
This is an early investment.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.500
A temporary rental.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.510
Are you sure?

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.510
Just don't die on me.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.620
I'll lose out on the tab.

00:17:58.620 --> 00:17:59.880
Besides...

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.150
What?

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:02.510
Let's talk inside.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:07.770
Gayus, where did you find this?

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.850
It's a rotten gift left 
behind by a man I despise.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.980
Apparently it's called an Eye of the Cosmos.

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:16.360
Eye of the Cosmos?

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.000
And the results of the analysis?

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:23.100
I didn't find much, but this carving is made

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:28.040
from the scales of a dragon that's 
been alive for over 10,000 years.

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:29.720
Ten thousand years?

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:32.420
That's way more than a 1,000-year class Altar.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:36.200
Yeah, this dragon far outranks that.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:37.920
I've tried running this red rock

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:41.530
through all kinds of analysis equipment,
 but it's unidentifiable.

00:18:41.530 --> 00:18:46.780
Though there was a report that something's 
been seen pulsating within the gem.

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:47.930
What do you mean?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:52.080
Put simply, this ring is alive.

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:53.310
Alive?

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:55.570
I say this for your sake.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:59.450
You ought to give this 
back to that man you hate.

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:07.380
Good for you.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.200
It's so peaceful.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.210
Yeah.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:17.130
Maybe I should have bought 
some for Gigina, too.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:20.140
He says he doesn't want any.

00:19:20.140 --> 00:19:21.470
Don't mind him.

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.050
I know, but...

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:28.280
Jiv...

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:29.980
Gayus. What a coincidence.

00:19:30.450 --> 00:19:31.780
Largonkin.

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:35.040
Jivenya, was it?

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:36.500
What a nice lady.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.480
Yeah, she's a great woman.

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:42.400
Do you not have plans to 
start a family with her?

00:19:42.400 --> 00:19:44.150
Family is great.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:46.980
I'm not like you.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:50.910
I don't know when I might die
 in my line of work.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:53.000
I live desperately.

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:57.510
A happy life seems like nothing 
but far-off make-believe.

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.100
You're so young.

00:20:01.060 --> 00:20:04.890
Forget about Cuello already.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:06.260
Largonkin!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.870
Diorg is dead.

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:14.500
Stratos is without a soul.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.270
Cuello is gone.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.620
Gigina and I were left with the agency.

00:20:20.620 --> 00:20:21.780
That's all.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.470
Looks like another Magatsushiki showed up.

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:34.560
Gigina.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:35.780
You don't need to come.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:39.970
You won't be useful in your current state.

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:53.540
You smell nice.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:56.600
Desire No. 9 by Algamon?

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:01.660
I don't trust men who 
know a lot about perfume.

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:04.200
Doesn't that mean...

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:08.820
It's a requirement of a kind man.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:18.710
<i>I see.</i>

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.140
<i>I'm...</i>

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.860
I was thinking about the past.

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:35.480
There was a time that I 
considered myself happy,

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:38.190
when I had people I could call friends.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.860
I'd forgotten until today.

00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:44.200
No, I think I wanted to forget.

00:21:46.120 --> 00:21:47.220
Why?

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:50.300
I don't care to answer my prey's questions.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:57.050
<i>Cuello... Where did we go wrong?</i>

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:03.760
Jiv, what's wrong?

00:22:04.220 --> 00:22:08.010
What did Largonkin tell you earlier today?

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:11.100
Nothing.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:13.010
We were just talking about
 silly stuff from the past.

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:15.270
It was about that Cuello person, wasn't it?

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:18.880
The person who used to wear 
Desire No. 9 before I did.

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:23.160
You called me Cuello in your sleep, Gayus.

00:22:24.550 --> 00:22:26.530
Jiv, that's...

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:27.930
Why?

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:31.280
Why won't you look at the here and now? At me?

00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:33.960
What are you really looking at?

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:36.330
Is it something we can't share?

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:38.250
Is it something you can share with Gigina?

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:40.990
Or with this Cuello person?

00:22:40.990 --> 00:22:42.290
Jiv...

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:45.510
Go home for the night.

00:22:45.970 --> 00:22:46.970
Please.

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:53.000
<i>Badass.</i>

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.940
<i>You're a real badass, Gayus.</i>

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:58.310
<i>You get a few old scars dug up, 
and look at you now.</i>

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:01.230
<i>No matter how hard I try to forget,</i>

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:04.650
<i>my past is still there,</i>

00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:07.400
<i>questioning me.</i>

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.820
<i>Asking if I made the right choice.</i>

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:13.050
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:18.320
<i>You're so badass, Gayus.</i>

00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:20.330
<i>You might as well die.</i>

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:33.790
I see.

00:23:33.790 --> 00:23:34.780
Well done.

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:41.600
I can't help but hate myself 
on nights like these.

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:54.200
A kind angel flies into the sky,
 trying to save the earth.

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:56.740
Because they flew at a height 
that people could reach,

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:00.620
the angel of salvation's wings and 
flesh became the people's desire,

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:04.060
until there wasn't a single feather left.

00:24:02.620 --> 00:24:05.130
<b>Revelation of Malice</b>
